  "details": "Sometimes the sound indication for a chatbox is simply too little, and you can miss a mute's entire message when its too crowded, sometimes you try to communicate with a deaf player and dont know ASL, but if they're not explicitly paying attention to the chatbox, they might miss what you say, it would be nice to have a feature which can point you in the direction of a chatbox without the need for playing charades to get someone to notice it. What comes to mind to me immediately is something similar to the system fortnite uses, a radial of some sort, maybe attatched to the hand or in the middle of the screen in desktop mode, where it points in a direction around a circle or, it can highlight an edge of your screen, in the direction it came from to point you in the right direction.",
